<%# A spot session sitting in the queue rather than running, in any of the four
    ways it gets there: held at the starting line (a quota window at its target,
    or no free session slot), held before its NEXT turn when a wake or a
    follow-up arrived while a window was at its target, paused mid-run once a
    window arrived at its target with this session already running, or put there
    deliberately with `action_session`'s "pause_into_spot_queue". Without this
    the session sits in `waiting` looking indistinguishable from one that is
    merely queued, and the only record of why would be a line in its log.

    One partial for all four because a session is only ever in one of them, and
    they are ordered most-specific first: a deliberate park describes the session
    better than the gate reason layered on top of it. %>
<%# The hold, read through SpotSessionHold::Record rather than key by key, so
    the two sentences this banner needs — how old the reading is, and whether the
    re-check it promises is still coming — are the SAME sentences `get_session`
    prints. A hold detail is a snapshot taken at `spot_hold_at`, and rendering it
    with nothing to say so is how session 7507's page told a human "5 of 5
    session slots taken" eleven hours after that stopped being true. %>
<% hold = SpotSessionHold.record_for(agent_session) %>
<% hold_detail = hold&.detail %>
<% hold_reason = hold&.reason %>
<%# A hold on a RESUME is a turn that was refused, not a session that never
    started: the session has run before and is waiting to run its next turn. %>
<% held_turn = hold&.turn %>
<% pause_detail = agent_session.metadata&.dig(SpotSessionPause::PAUSED_DETAIL) %>
<%# The ranking, shared with `get_session`, so a human on this page and an agent
    reading the MCP tool are never told about two different mechanisms. It answers
    two questions this box could not answer for itself: which of a hold and a
    pause it is about when the row carries both, and whether the spot mechanism is
    why the session is waiting AT ALL — an auth-outage park recorded later has a
    different owner (the pool's recovery), and the box above is then the real
    reason. See SessionWaitingReason and tadasant/zimmer#642. %>
<% waiting_reason = SessionWaitingReason.for(agent_session) %>
<% spot_reason = waiting_reason&.spot %>
<%# Gated on the ranking, not on the metadata keys: a box drawn without a ranked
    mechanism would be a box that bypassed the precedence, which is the bug. Both
    writers of `spot_pause_detail` write `spot_pause_reason` in the same hash
    (SpotSessionPause#pause!, Sessions::PauseIntoSpotQueue), so there is no row
    with one and not the other for this to lock out. %>
<% if spot_reason && (hold_detail.present? || pause_detail.present?) %>
  <% paused_mid_run = spot_reason.key == SessionWaitingReason::SPOT_PAUSE || hold_detail.blank? %>
  <% superseded_by_park = !waiting_reason.current?(spot_reason) %>
  <%# A third case shares the pause record: a session parked in the queue
      deliberately. Nothing interrupted it and no turn was lost, so it gets its
      own sentence rather than being described as a casualty of the ceiling. %>
  <% queued_by_user = SpotSessionPause.queued_by_user?(agent_session) %>
  <%# A data attribute rather than an id: this partial renders twice per page —
      once in the mobile block, once in the desktop header, mirroring
      auth_outage_banner — and two elements cannot share one id. %>
  <div class="mb-4 rounded-md border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4" data-spot-hold-banner>
    <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-amber-500 shrink-0 mt-0.5" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
        <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm1-11a1 1 0 10-2 0v4a1 1 0 00.293.707l2 2a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11 10.586V7z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
      </svg>
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-amber-900">
          <% if queued_by_user %>
            Waiting in the spot queue
          <% elsif paused_mid_run %>
            Paused mid-run for quota headroom
          <% elsif hold&.overdue? %>
            <%# The headline stops claiming a live ceiling once the re-check it
                rests on has come and gone: at that point the session is not
                being held by anything, it is waiting on a job that never ran. %>
            Spot hold stalled — its re-check never fired
          <% elsif hold_reason == "fleet_at_cap" %>
            Held for a free session slot
          <% elsif held_turn == SpotSessionHold::TURN_RESUME %>
            Next turn held for quota headroom
          <% else %>
            Held for quota headroom
          <% end %>
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-amber-800"><%= paused_mid_run ? pause_detail : hold_detail %></p>
        <%# Said before the resume prose below, which describes THIS mechanism's
            owner and would otherwise send the reader to the wrong one. %>
        <% if superseded_by_park %>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-amber-900" data-spot-hold-superseded>
            <% if spot_reason.demoted? %>
              This is not why the session is waiting now: the account pool is what it is waiting on, and
              nothing is coming to re-arm this hold — the spot-hold sweep skips a session that also
              carries an auth-outage park.
            <% else %>
              This is not why the session is waiting now: the auth-outage park above was recorded later,
              and the account pool is what it is waiting on.
            <% end %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
        <%# The age of the sentence above, always, and never as an afterthought:
            without it a reader has no way to tell an eleven-hour-old gate
            reading from a live one. %>
        <% if !paused_mid_run && hold&.as_of_sentence %>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-amber-700" data-spot-hold-as-of>
            <%= hold.as_of_sentence %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-amber-700">
          This is a <span class="font-medium">spot</span> session
          (genesis <span class="font-mono"><%= agent_session.genesis_key %></span>,
          <%= agent_session.scheduling_class_source %>). It has not been cancelled —
          <%# Every clause below names what THIS mechanism's owner will do, so a
              superseded box must not reach them: they would send the reader to the
              spot gate for a session the account pool is holding. %>
          <% if superseded_by_park %>
            it resumes from the outage above, once the account pool recovers.
          <% elsif queued_by_user %>
            it was parked in the queue deliberately, with no wake-up time, and it resumes
            when a Claude account is under both quota targets and a slot is free, ahead of everything
            ranked below precedence <%= agent_session.precedence %>.
          <% elsif paused_mid_run %>
            it was already running when a window reached its target, and it resumes on its own
            once utilization falls <%= SpotGateService::RESUME_MARGIN_PCT %> points below it.
          <% elsif held_turn == SpotSessionHold::TURN_RESUME %>
            the turn it was woken for is queued and runs on its own once the gate lets it.
          <% else %>
            it will start on its own once the gate lets it.
          <% end %>
        </p>
        <%# What happens next, stated as what it IS. An overdue re-check is named
            as overdue and paired with the sweep that repairs it, rather than
            printed as a time that has already passed and reads as upcoming.
            Dropped entirely once a later auth-outage park supersedes the hold: the
            sweep this sentence promises skips such a session, so the promise would
            be false. %>
        <% if !paused_mid_run && hold && !superseded_by_park %>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs <%= hold.overdue? ? "font-medium text-amber-900" : "text-amber-700" %>" data-spot-hold-recheck>
            <%= hold.recheck_sentence %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
        <%# Moves this session alone. The genesis-wide lever on /inference would
            move every other session that shares its origin, which is exactly the
            blast radius that made it the wrong tool for one held session. %>
        <%= button_to "Make this session priority",
              update_scheduling_class_session_path(agent_session, scheduling_class: SessionGenesis::PRIORITY),
              method: :patch,
              form: { data: { turbo: false }, class: "mt-2" },
              class: "inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-amber-900 shadow-sm hover:bg-amber-100 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-amber-500 focus:ring-offset-1" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
